            <h3>High-Speed vs Regional Trains</h3>
            <p>High-Speed (Acela): While not true European-style high-speed rail, the Acela operates at speeds up to 150 mph on certain segments of the Northeast Corridor, making it the fastest option between Baltimore and Wilmington. The Acela offers a premium experience with leather seating, quiet cars, and complimentary beverages.</p>

            <p>Regional Trains (Northeast Regional): These services operate at lower speeds with more frequent stops but offer greater affordability and accessibility. The Northeast Regional provides a comfortable intercity experience with all the essential amenities.</p>

